ecause we checked budget <= total capacity, but after minima, if remaining > 0 and all segments are at capacity, that means total capacity = sum minima, so budget <= total capacity but budget > sum minima? Actually if total capacity = sum minima, then budget cannot be > sum minima because budget <= total capacity, so remaining = 0. So it's fine.\n\nNow, the implementation must be inside a Python source string. Also note: the eval environment uses the JSON string.\n\nWe need to output exactly one JSON object with key \"implementation\" and value is a JSON-escaped string of the Python source.\n\nWe'll write the function with proper indentation, escape newlines as \\n, backslashes \\\\, quotes \\\".\n\nLet's produce the response.\n\nBut note: The user message says \"Do not use Markdown code fences.\" So we output raw JSON.\n\nThus, build the JSON.\n\nImplementation code:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    segments = case[\"segments\"]\n    budget = case[\"budget\"]\n    min_sum = sum(seg[\"minimum\"] for seg in segments)\n    cap_sum = sum(seg[\"capacity\"] for seg in segments)\n    if budget < min_sum or budget > cap_sum:\n        raise ValueError(\"Budget not feasible\")\n    allocs = [seg[\"minimum\"] for seg in segments]\n    remaining = budget - min_sum\n    from fractions import Fraction\n    while remaining > 0:\n        best_idx = None\n        best_frac = None\n        for i, seg in enumerate(segments):\n            if allocs[i] < seg[\"capacity\"]:\n                frac = Fraction(seg[\"importance\"], allocs[i] + 1)\n                if best_idx is None or frac > best_frac:\n                    best_frac = frac\n                    best_idx = i\n        if best_idx is None:\n            # should not happen because budget <= cap, but just in case\n            raise ValueError(\"Insufficient capacity\")\n        allocs[best_idx] += 1\n        remaining -= 1\n    by_name = {seg[\"name\"]: allocs[i] for i, seg in enumerate(segments)}\n    total = sum(allocs)\n    return {\"